  "wikitext": "{{Short description|Species of moss}}\n{{Speciesbox\n| image = Neckera pennata (c, 144615-474707) 2631.JPG\n| genus = Neckera\n| species = pennata\n| authority = Hedwig, 1801\n}}\n\n'''''Neckera pennata''''' is a species of [[moss]] belonging to the family [[Neckeraceae]].<ref name=\"GBIF\">{{cite web |title=Neckera pennata Hedwig, 1801 |url=https://www.gbif.org/species/2678586 |website=www.gbif.org |access-date=12 February 2021 |language=en}}</ref>\n\nIt has a [[cosmopolitan distribution]].<ref name=\"GBIF\" /> Feather flat moss can be an indicator of late successional and old-growth hardwood forests, because it usually grows on sugar maples in the Northeast that are at least 120 years old.{{cn|date=November 2021}}\n\n==References==\n{{Reflist}}\n\n{{Taxonbar|from=Q310593}}\n\n[[Category:Neckeraceae]]",
